  (3, 'first', 'The quiet beginning', 'You do not have to feel different yet for this to be real.', 'Begin the few early habits that matter — without trying to feel pregnant.', 'By standard due-date counting, the first two weeks occur before conception. Fertilisation and implantation may happen later in this grouped period. Many people have no symptoms, and symptoms do not reliably predict pregnancy health.', ARRAY['No noticeable changes','Mild cramping or light spotting around implantation — or neither','Breast tenderness, tiredness or bloating','A missed period near the end of this stage']::text[], '{"focus": "Continue movement that already feels familiar; this is not the time to prove or suddenly transform fitness.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Walk gently for 3 minutes, then roll your shoulders and circle your ankles for 2 minutes.", "steady": "Take a 10-minute conversational walk, then spend 5 minutes on calf stretches, shoulder rolls and easy side-to-side weight shifts.", "feeling_good": "Choose 20 minutes of familiar moderate activity, then complete one easy round of 8 chair sit-to-stands, 8 wall push-ups and 10 heel raises."}, "mood_adjustment": "Uncertain or newly testing: choose familiar movement. Crampy or tired: use five minutes or rest. Feeling normal and well: continue your usual moderate option without overheating.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'If pregnancy is possible, take a prenatal vitamin containing folic acid as advised locally. Build meals from familiar foods; perfection is neither necessary nor possible.', 'Keep water nearby and drink regularly. Hydration needs vary with climate, activity and health conditions.', '{"heavy_day": "If uncertainty feels overwhelming, narrow the day to the next hour. Eat, drink, rest or contact someone safe — which