  (4, 'first', 'The quiet beginning', 'You do not have to feel different yet for this to be real.', 'Begin the few early habits that matter — without trying to feel pregnant.', 'By standard due-date counting, the first two weeks occur before conception. Fertilisation and implantation may happen later in this grouped period. Many people have no symptoms, and symptoms do not reliably predict pregnancy health.', ARRAY['No noticeable changes','Mild cramping or light spotting around implantation — or neither','Breast tenderness, tiredness or bloating','A missed period near the end of this stage']::text[], '{"focus": "Continue movement that already feels familiar; this is not the time to prove or suddenly transform fitness.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Walk gently for 3 minutes, then roll your shoulders and circle your ankles for 2 minutes.", "steady": "Take a 10-minute conversational walk, then spend 5 minutes on calf stretches, shoulder rolls and easy side-to-side weight shifts.", "feeling_good": "Choose 20 minutes of familiar moderate activity, then complete one easy round of 8 chair sit-to-stands, 8 wall push-ups and 10 heel raises."}, "mood_adjustment": "Uncertain or newly testing: choose familiar movement. Crampy or tired: use five minutes or rest. Feeling normal and well: continue your usual moderate option without overheating.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'If pregnancy is possible, take a prenatal vitamin containing folic acid as advised locally. Build meals from familiar foods; perfection is neither necessary nor possible.', 'Keep water nearby and drink regularly. Hydration needs vary with climate, activity and health conditions.', '{"heavy_day": "If uncertainty feels overwhelming, narrow the day to the next hour. Eat, drink, rest or contact someone safe — whichever need comes first.", "a_little_low": "Say: \"Not knowing yet is uncomfortable, and I do not have to solve it all today.\" Step away from repeated searching for ten minutes.", "okay": "Write down the date you plan to test or contact your clinician. Once the next step is clear, return to ordinary life.", "good": "Use the steadier mood to prepare one supportive habit: a vitamin reminder, an easy breakfast or a saved clinic number.", "really_good": "Let hope exist without demanding certainty. Record one sentence about how this beginning feels and keep it private if you prefer."}'::jsonb, 'Use a simple skin routine and check medicines, supplements or strong skincare actives with a qualified clinician or pharmacist rather than stopping prescribed treatment on your own.', 'Save one small memory from this beginning — a date, a photo, a private thought or nothing at all.', 'If you are sharing the possibility with someone, tell them what support would help: calm company, practical help or simply privacy.', 'Every pregnancy begins quietly. You do not need symptoms or certainty to deserve care.', 'Seek urgent care for severe or one-sided pain, shoulder-tip pain, fainting, heavy bleeding, fever or feeling seriously unwell.'),
  (5, 'first', 'Your body is changing faster than it looks', 'Small meals, small steps and small wins all count.', 'Respond to nausea and fatigue without guilt.', 'Pregnancy hormones are rising quickly. Nausea, food aversions and exhaustion may begin — or you may still feel little change. The early foundations of the brain, spinal cord and heart are developing.', ARRAY['Nausea with or without vomiting','Food or smell aversions','Sore breasts, bloating or frequent urination','Fatigue — or no symptoms yet']::text[], '{"focus": "Use short, gentle movement to support mood and circulation without worsening nausea.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Walk slowly for 3 minutes, then take 2 minutes for shoulder rolls and relaxed breathing.", "steady": "Walk for 8-10 minutes at an easy pace. Add 5 minutes of ankle circles, calf stretching and gentle wall pelvic tilts.", "feeling_good": "Walk for 15-20 minutes, then complete one to two easy rounds of 8 chair sit-to-stands, 8 wall push-ups and 10 heel raises."}, "mood_adjustment": "Nauseated: move when symptoms are usually lowest and keep a snack nearby. Exhausted: five minutes or rest. Anxious: choose a familiar route. Feeling good: finish with energy left.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'Eat what you can tolerate. Try small, frequent meals and bland or cool foods if helpful. Pair easy carbohydrates with protein when possible; continue prescribed prenatal supplements.', 'Take small, frequent sips if larger drinks trigger nausea. Ice, a straw, diluted flavours or oral rehydration advice from your clinician may help.', '{"heavy_day": "Make the next ten minutes about survival, not self-improvement. Reduce smells and noise, take small sips and lie or sit somewhere supported.", "a_little_low": "If you feel disappointed by your capacity, say: \"My body is working hard even when today looks small.\" Remove one nonessential task.", "okay": "Notice the time when nausea or energy is usually easiest. Protect that window for food, washing or one necessary activity.", "good": "Use the steadier moment to prepare tomorrow''s easiest snack or refill your bedside water. Stop before preparation becomes a project.", "really_good": "Enjoy the relief without trying to catch up on everything. Choose one pleasant activity and keep the rest of the day spacious."}'::jsonb, 'Switch to fragrance-free products if smells are triggering. A soft toothbrush, bland toothpaste or rinsing after vomiting may make mouth care easier.', 'Record today''s easiest food, funniest aversion or one sentence about what surprised you.', 'Ask someone else to handle one smell-heavy task, meal or errand.', 'You adapted instead of forcing. That is effective care.', 'Contact your clinician if you cannot keep fluids down, urinate very little, feel faint, vomit blood or have severe pain, fever or bleeding.'),
  (6, 'first', 'Rest is productive', 'Exhaustion is not a character flaw.', 'Protect energy and begin organising prenatal care.', 'The placenta is developing and hormonal changes can feel intense. Fatigue may be profound, while nausea, breast tenderness, bloating and emotional swings can grow stronger.', ARRAY['Heavy fatigue or needing more sleep','Nausea, vomiting or strong smell sensitivity','Mood changes','Light cramping without severe pain — or none']::text[], '{"focus": "Keep movement restorative and reduce the plan before your body has to demand it.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Walk for 2 minutes, then do 8 ankle circles per side, 6 wall pelvic tilts and three slow breaths.", "steady": "Walk for 8 minutes. Add one gentle round of 8 wall push-ups, 8 heel raises and 8 chair sit-to-stands.", "feeling_good": "Choose 15-20 minutes of conversational walking, swimming or stationary cycling. Add 10 minutes of easy mobility and supported strength."}, "mood_adjustment": "Depleted: choose five minutes or sleep. Nauseated: avoid an empty stomach if that worsens symptoms. Restless: use rhythmic walking. Energised: stay moderate rather than using the day to compensate.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'Plan one reliable protein option and one easy carbohydrate. Curd with fruit, eggs and toast, dal-rice, nut butter and toast, or roasted chana may suit different tolerances.', 'Keep drinks within reach of where you rest. Small sips throughout the day count.', '{"heavy_day": "Close your eyes, soften your jaw and allow ten minutes without conversation, scrolling or decisions. Rest is the intervention today.", "a_little_low": "Name what tiredness is making harder. Ask for help with that exact thing rather than waiting until everything feels impossible.", "okay": "Choose one priority for the day and deliberately label the rest \"optional.\" Let the list reflect your actual energy.", "good": "Use the steadier window for one practical task, then schedule recovery immediately afterwards instead of waiting to crash.", "really_good": "Spend some energy on enjoyment, not only catching up. Stop while you still feel well."}'::jsonb, 'Make rest easier: dim light, cool room, comfortable layers and a pillow where you need support. Daytime rest is not failure.', 'Create a two-item "low-energy menu": one meal and one activity you can manage on difficult days.', 'Ask your support person to take full ownership of one recurring task this week.', 'You rested before reaching empty. That was wise.', 'Arrange prenatal care according to your local pathway. Seek urgent help for severe pain, heavy bleeding, fainting, fever or dehydration.'),
  (7, 'first', 'Eat what works today', 'Nutrition can be flexible while symptoms are loud.', 'Keep food and fluids manageable rather than idealised.', 'Nausea and food aversions often become more noticeable around this stage. Your baby''s early brain and facial structures are developing rapidly, even though pregnancy remains invisible from the outside.', ARRAY['Nausea at any time of day','Metallic taste, excess saliva or smell sensitivity','Constipation or bloating','Fatigue and emotional irritability']::text[], '{"focus": "Choose movement around symptom windows and avoid heat, hunger and sudden intensity.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Walk gently for 3 minutes in fresh or well-ventilated air, then stretch your calves for 1 minute per side.", "steady": "Walk for 10 minutes. Add 5 minutes of wall push-ups, heel raises and shoulder rolls.", "feeling_good": "Walk or use a stationary cycle for 20 minutes at conversational effort. Add one round of 8 chair sit-to-stands, 8 wall push-ups and 10 heel raises."}, "mood_adjustment": "Queasy: choose cool air, a short route and five minutes. Irritable: move without instruction or tracking. Okay: use 15 minutes. Feeling good: choose 30 minutes but stop before hunger or fatigue spikes.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'Try small portions every few hours. Cold or room-temperature foods may smell less intense. Ginger may help some people, but check concentrated supplements with your clinician.', 'If plain water is difficult, try chilled water, diluted juice, soup or other pregnancy-safe fluids that suit you. Ask for help early if intake is falling.', '{"heavy_day": "Reduce sensory load: move away from cooking smells, lower the lights and take slow sips. Your job is comfort, not productivity.", "a_little_low": "If food feels like a daily battle, release the idea of a beautiful plate. One tolerated food is still useful information.", "okay": "List three foods and two drinks that usually stay down. Keep the list visible so decisions require less energy.", "good": "Use the calmer window to stock one easy food for tomorrow. Preparation can be tiny and still reduce stress.", "really_good": "Enjoy whatever feels appealing without analysing whether it is \"pregnancy perfect.\" Pleasure and nourishment can coexist."}'::jsonb, 'Keep a bland mouth rinse or toothpaste option available. Wait before brushing immediately after vomiting; rinse first and follow dental advice.', 'Save your current safest snack or drink as a quick-access favourite in the app.', 'Let someone else cook, order or clean up. Tell them which smells currently need to stay away.', 'You fed and hydrated the body you have today — not an imaginary one.', 'Persistent vomiting is treatable. Contact your clinician early if symptoms limit eating, drinking, urination, daily function or weight maintenance.'),
  (8, 'first', 'Care can include appointments', 'You do not need to arrive with every question answered.', 'Prepare for early prenatal assessment without letting it consume the week.', 'Your baby''s limbs and major body systems are developing. Prenatal appointment timing varies by country, history and individual needs; some people have already been seen while others are booking now.', ARRAY['Strong fatigue, nausea or breast tenderness','Frequent urination','Vivid dreams or emotional sensitivity','Worry before an appointment or scan']::text[], '{"focus": "Use familiar movement to regulate appointment anxiety and maintain comfort.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Take a 5-minute slow walk while relaxing your hands and shoulders.", "steady": "Walk for 10 minutes, then do 5 minutes of ankle circles, wall pelvic tilts and gentle side stretches.", "feeling_good": "Choose 20 minutes of familiar moderate activity. Add 10 minutes of supported strength: wall push-ups, chair sit-to-stands and heel raises."}, "mood_adjustment": "Anxious: choose repetition and familiarity. Symptom-heavy: five minutes or rest. Mentally tired: no new exercises. Feeling good: complete the longer option without turning it into proof that everything is okay.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'Prepare one appointment-day food that travels safely and sits well. Keep prenatal vitamins and prescribed medicines on your question list if they are hard to tolerate.', 'Ask your clinic whether a full bladder or fasting is needed for any test; otherwise follow your usual hydration routine.', '{"heavy_day": "If appointment fear is overwhelming, identify the next factual step: call, confirm, attend or ask. You do not need to emotionally solve the whole pregnancy.", "a_little_low": "Write the question beneath the worry. Clear questions create more support than repeated searching.", "okay": "Prepare your records, medication list and three questions. Once ready, close the notes and return to today.", "good": "Plan one comforting thing after the appointment: food, rest, company or quiet. Care includes the landing afterwards.", "really_good": "Let excitement be present without demanding reassurance from every sensation. Save one hopeful thought and continue your day."}'::jsonb, 'Choose comfortable clothing and bring any records requested. If examinations or procedures feel difficult, tell the clinician what helps you feel informed and in control.', 'Record your top three appointment questions in one place.', 'Invite a support person if you want and the clinic allows it. Tell them whether their role is reassurance, transport or note-taking.', 'You prepared for care without needing to become the expert.', 'Ask how results will be communicated, what symptoms need urgent attention and when your next contact is expected.'),
  (9, 'first', 'Surviving counts', 'This week does not have to look graceful.', 'Lower expectations while symptoms may be near their loudest.', 'Hormonal levels remain high and symptoms can dominate daily life. Your baby''s early organs continue developing, but the care chart stays focused on helping you function and feel supported.', ARRAY['Nausea, vomiting or food aversions','Exhaustion and reduced concentration','Headaches or dizziness','Constipation, bloating or heartburn']::text[], '{"focus": "Treat movement as optional support, not another demand.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Walk for 3 minutes, then sit and take six relaxed breaths. Stop there if that is the right amount.", "steady": "Walk for 8 minutes at an easy pace. Add one round of 8 wall push-ups, 8 heel raises and gentle shoulder circles.", "feeling_good": "Choose 15-20 minutes of moderate walking, swimming or stationary cycling. Add 10 minutes of easy supported strength and mobility."}, "mood_adjustment": "Overwhelmed: five minutes or rest. Dizzy: sit, hydrate and seek advice if persistent — do not exercise through it. Flat: one song and a short walk. Good: enjoy moderate movement without catching up.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'Build a "survival menu" of tolerated foods. Add protein or fibre where you can, but do not withhold food until the ideal option appears.', 'Use regular small sips and monitor whether you are urinating normally. Ask your clinician about safe nausea treatment rather than waiting for dehydration.', '{"heavy_day": "Make the environment smaller: low light, fewer smells, phone away and one basic need at a time. Today can be about getting through.", "a_little_low": "Say: \"Reduced capacity is a symptom, not a personal failure.\" Cancel or delegate one task that can wait.", "okay": "Choose a minimum viable day: fluids, food, medicines as directed, hygiene and rest. Anything else is additional.", "good": "Use the steadier window for one helpful preparation, then stop before the good hour becomes an exhausting one.", "really_good": "Let the better mood be enjoyable rather than productive. Do something that reminds you that you are still yourself."}'::jsonb, 'A lukewarm shower, loose clothing, a cool cloth or fragrance-free products may reduce sensory discomfort.', 'Create a private "I got through today" note using one sentence or one photo.', 'Give your support person a short list of tasks they can do without asking you to manage them.', 'You kept showing up during a demanding week. That is enough.', 'Seek advice for persistent or severe headache, fainting, reduced urination, inability to keep fluids down, severe pain, fever or bleeding.'),
  (10, 'first', 'Adapt, do not force', 'Your routine is allowed to change before your bump does.', 'Support posture, digestion and daily function with small adjustments.', 'The placenta is taking on more of its role, though symptoms may continue. Your uterus is growing, and bloating can make the abdomen feel different from one day to another.', ARRAY['Bloating, constipation or heartburn','Fatigue that comes in waves','Tight clothing before a clear bump','Emotional relief, worry or both']::text[], '{"focus": "Build basic strength and mobility with supported, controlled movement.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Do 6 wall pelvic tilts, 8 heel raises and 6 wall push-ups with relaxed breathing.", "steady": "Complete two rounds of 8 wall pelvic tilts, 8 wall push-ups, 8 chair sit-to-stands and 10 heel raises.", "feeling_good": "Warm up with a 10-minute walk. Complete two rounds of 10 wall pelvic tilts, 10 wall push-ups, 8 chair sit-to-stands and 10 heel raises. Cool down gently."}, "mood_adjustment": "Sore or bloated: choose walking and mobility. Nervous about exercise: use stable support and a small range. Steady: complete 15 minutes. Energised: complete 30 at conversational effort.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'Support digestion with fibre plus fluid: oats, fruit, vegetables, whole grains, lentils and beans. Increase fibre gradually if your intake has been low.', 'Spread drinks through the day. If heartburn is troublesome, smaller amounts more often may feel better than large drinks with meals.', '{"heavy_day": "Release the need to maintain your old routine. Choose the most comfortable clothing and remove one physical or mental pressure point.", "a_little_low": "Name one change that is frustrating you. Respond with adjustment rather than criticism: rest, different food, softer clothing or help.", "okay": "Take a two-minute posture reset: feet supported, jaw soft, shoulders easy. Comfort is a valid outcome.", "good": "Use the steadier mood to improve one repeated routine — your work chair, bedside water or snack location.", "really_good": "Notice one adaptation that is already helping. Let competence feel good without needing to add another goal."}'::jsonb, 'Choose softer waistbands and supportive, comfortable bras if needed. Skin and hair changes vary; there is nothing you need to fix this week.', 'Take a photo of something that made daily life easier.', 'Ask someone to help adjust a repeated routine — food prep, commuting, bedtime or household work.', 'You adapted before discomfort had to become a crisis.', 'Discuss persistent constipation, reflux, pain or symptoms that interfere with eating, sleeping or normal activity.'),
  (11, 'first', 'Questions belong in the room', 'Prepared does not mean perfectly calm.', 'Approach screening or appointments with informed choice and support.', 'Depending on your country and preferences, first-trimester screening or diagnostic discussions may occur around this stage. Testing options, timing and meaning should be explained by a qualified clinician.', ARRAY['Continuing symptoms or the first signs of easing','Anxiety about tests or results','Headaches, dizziness or nasal congestion','A changing appetite']::text[], '{"focus": "Use movement to settle your body — not to control an appointment outcome.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Walk slowly for 5 minutes and keep your attention on your surroundings rather than your thoughts.", "steady": "Walk for 10 minutes. Add 5 minutes of shoulder rolls, wall pelvic tilts and calf stretching.", "feeling_good": "Choose 20 minutes of conversational aerobic activity, then one easy round of chair sit-to-stands, wall push-ups and heel raises."}, "mood_adjustment": "Worried: choose familiar, rhythmic movement. Tired after blood tests or appointments: rest. Okay: use 15 minutes. Feeling good: keep the longer routine moderate and well hydrated.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'Take an easy snack and water to appointments if allowed. Continue normal eating unless the clinic gives specific fasting instructions.', 'Confirm preparation instructions with the clinic rather than guessing. Bring water for afterwards if permitted.', '{"heavy_day": "If testing decisions feel overwhelming, pause and ask for an explanation in plain language. You are allowed time and questions.", "a_little_low": "Write what you fear the result might mean, then write the factual question your clinician can answer.", "okay": "Prepare three questions: What does this test screen for? What can the result tell me? What happens next?", "good": "Use the steadier mood to organise records and transport, then deliberately stop researching for the day.", "really_good": "Let confidence come from informed choice, not certainty. Mark the appointment as one caring step in a longer journey."}'::jsonb, 'Take a notebook or use your phone for notes. Ask permission before recording and request written information where available.', 'Save the question you most want answered — not the question you think you are supposed to ask.', 'Tell your support person whether you want them to ask questions, take notes or simply stay close.', 'You advocated for understanding. That matters.', 'Ask about the benefits, limits and possible next steps of any screening or diagnostic test before deciding.'),
  (12, 'first', 'Reassurance can arrive slowly', 'Feeling less anxious is not a requirement for progress.', 'Make space for changing symptoms and changing emotions.', 'Some people begin to feel more energetic or less nauseated; others do not. As pregnancy progresses, the likelihood of miscarriage becomes lower, but reassurance and attachment arrive differently for everyone.', ARRAY['Symptoms easing, continuing or fluctuating','A slightly firmer lower abdomen','Headaches, dizziness or constipation','Relief mixed with lingering worry']::text[], '{"focus": "Rebuild consistency gently if energy begins to return.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Walk for 3 minutes, then complete 6 chair sit-to-stands and 6 wall push-ups.", "steady": "Walk for 8 minutes. Add two rounds of 8 chair sit-to-stands, 8 wall push-ups and 10 heel raises.", "feeling_good": "Walk, swim or cycle for 20 minutes. Add one to two easy rounds of 10 chair sit-to-stands, 10 wall push-ups and 10 heel raises."}, "mood_adjustment": "Still symptomatic: stay with five minutes. Cautiously hopeful: choose familiar movement. Okay: use 15 minutes. Energised: increase duration gradually rather than jumping back to an old routine.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'If appetite is returning, rebuild variety gradually. Aim for regular meals with protein, fibre and colour, while keeping tolerated fallback foods available.', 'Continue regular fluids even if nausea improves. Drink before, during and after movement.', '{"heavy_day": "If fear remains loud, do not argue with it. Put both feet down, lengthen your exhale and choose one trustworthy source of support.", "a_little_low": "Remind yourself: symptom changes are common, and worry is not intuition. Contact your clinician if something specific concerns you.", "okay": "Name what feels different this week without deciding whether it is good or bad. Observation can stay neutral.", "good": "Use the steadier mood to acknowledge one thing that has become easier and one support you want to continue.", "really_good": "Enjoy relief without feeling guilty or needing to announce it. Joy can be quiet and provisional."}'::jsonb, 'Continue simple skincare and sunscreen. Ask before using prescription or high-strength active ingredients during pregnancy.', 'Write or record: "What I want to remember about the end of this trimester."', 'Share one thing that has become easier and one worry you still need handled gently.', 'You have reached a meaningful point without needing to feel only one emotion.', 'Contact your clinician for bleeding, severe pain, fever, fainting, persistent vomiting or any symptom that feels suddenly or seriously wrong.'),
  (13, 'first', 'First-trimester graduation', 'Look how much you have already carried.', 'Close the trimester with reflection, recovery and a gentle look ahead.', 'You are approaching the second trimester. Symptoms may begin shifting, though fatigue or nausea can continue. Your baby''s major structures are formed and will keep growing and maturing.', ARRAY['More energy — or no clear change yet','A growing abdomen or continued bloating','Changing appetite','Relief, pride, worry or emotional neutrality']::text[], '{"focus": "Choose a routine you can carry forward and adapt rather than outgrow.", "tiers": {"heavy": "Choose your favourite two gentle movements from this trimester and do them for 5 minutes total.", "steady": "Walk for 7 minutes, then complete one round of 10 chair sit-to-stands, 10 wall push-ups and 10 heel raises.", "feeling_good": "Warm up for 5 minutes. Complete 15 minutes of walking, swimming or stationary cycling, then one to two easy strength rounds. Cool down for 5 minutes."}, "mood_adjustment": "Still unwell: choose comfort or rest. Proud but tired: take the five-minute option. Steady: use 15 minutes. Energised: repeat favourites without chasing pre-pregnancy performance.", "safety": "Use stable support, breathe continuously and keep effort conversational. Stop for pain, bleeding, dizziness, chest pain, breathlessness before exertion, fluid leakage, calf pain/swelling or anything that feels wrong."}'::jsonb, 'Create a second-trimester support list: three easy meals, three snacks and one person or service that can help when food remains difficult.', 'Refresh your routine by placing water where you rest, work and leave home. Continue any personalised advice.', '{"heavy_day": "You do not need to feel transformed at the trimester boundary. Choose one immediate comfort and let the next stage wait.", "a_little_low": "Name what this trimester cost you — energy, certainty, appetite or privacy. Your pride does not have to erase the difficulty.", "okay": "Review one thing that helped and one thing you want more support with. Keep the reflection practical.", "good": "Create a small first-trimester time capsule: one photo, one voice note and one thing you learned about yourself.", "really_good": "Mark the ending in a way that feels true — a meal, a walk, a private celebration or sharing the news if and when you choose."}'::jsonb, 'Do a comfort audit: bras, waistbands, sleep setup, work posture and products that now trigger sensitivity. Change one thing.', 'Save one memory that belongs to this trimester alone.', 'Have a gentle check-in about what support worked and what should change for the next trimester.', 'First trimester complete. Pause here before moving on — you have carried a great deal already.', 'Confirm upcoming appointments, local test or vaccine recommendations, medicine and supplement questions, and any ongoing symptoms.')
on conflict (week_number) do update set
  trimester = excluded.trimester,
  theme_title = excluded.theme_title,
  mantra = excluded.mantra,
  priority = excluded.priority,
  journey = excluded.journey,
  what_you_may_notice = excluded.what_you_may_notice,
  move = excluded.move,
  nourish = excluded.nourish,
  hydration_goal = excluded.hydration_goal,
  reset = excluded.reset,
  care_for_yourself = excluded.care_for_yourself,
  your_corner = excluded.your_corner,
  support_moment = excluded.support_moment,
  celebrate_this_week = excluded.celebrate_this_week,
  for_your_care_team = excluded.for_your_care_team;